comments.body:
Removing my `config.keys` override just makes option+left and option+right switch zellij tabs rather than move one word forward or backward, which isn't the desired behavior. Setting `config.enable_kitty_keyboard = true` doesn't seem to do anything. I can also replicate this with iterm2 that uses a similar mapping.

If anyone has the expected option+L/R behavior of moving by word, would you be able to share your configuration?

Also perhaps this issue should be reopened, a default keybinding that conflicts with `readline` commands is really unfortunate.

For reference, my current Wezterm configuration:

```lua
config.enable_kitty_keyboard = true

config.keys = {
  {
    key = 'LeftArrow',
    mods = 'ALT',
    action = wezterm.action.SendKey {
      key = 'b',
      mods = 'ALT',
    },
  },
  {
    key = 'RightArrow',
    mods = 'ALT',
    action = wezterm.action.SendKey {
      key = 'f',
      mods = 'ALT',
    },
  }
}
```

If anyone else needs it, I was able to fix this by unbinding on Zellij's side:

```kdl
keybindings {
    unbind "Alt f"
}
```
